    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #307\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-111-module-contract-05-12-run-resumable-mo-thr_ckbtz5nsbe` on origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis implements issue #111 ([module-contract 05/12] Run resumable module data migrations):\n\n- **Structural migration** `0011_module_data_migrations.sql`: adds `module_migrations(module_id, database_key, from_version, to_version, ran_at)` bookkeeping table and a nullable `databases.migration_cursor uuid` column (applied by the existing forward-only runner from #224). The migration file documents why the cursor lives on `databases` rather than the `properties` table the issue's DDL literally named — `properties` already carries an unrelated per-property `migration_status` from the existing single-property type-conversion feature, while a module data migration converts a whole database's items for one version-pair transition.\n- **`ModuleManifest.dataMigrations`** (module-registry package): a new descriptor (`databaseKey`, `fromVersion`, `toVersion`, `converterExport`), separate from the existing structural `migrations: string[]` field, with load-time validation (converter export must exist and be callable, `databaseKey` must belong to the module's own `databases`, no duplicate version-pair per key) and two new registry projections.\n- **`migrationJob/moduleDataMigration.ts`**: `runModuleDataMigration` executes one transition in id-ordered, resumable batches, committing the cursor after each successful batch; a converter failure rolls back only that batch, leaving the cursor at the last committed item. A session-level Postgres advisory lock plus the `module_migrations` primary key guard against the same transition running or being recorded twice. `runModuleDataMigrations` runs every migration a `ModuleRegistry` currently declares.\n- Full test coverage (registry validation/projections, plus integration tests for exactly-once conversion, crash-and-resume, already-recorded no-op, and concurrent-runner safety) and the whole backend test suite (417 tests) plus the full build were verified green before this push.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
